      <details class="result-details"><summary>How to use this funding path</summary><ol class="personal-steps"><li>Keep emergency cash and housing money accessible before funding long-term targets.</li><li>Check the ${money(t.cpfGap)} CPF target gap against your dashboard. The reserve is a funding equivalent at an assumed 4%, not an instruction to top up that amount every month. ERS may require holding money outside CPF until an eligible RA top-up or transfer after 55.</li><li>Fund the separate outside-CPF investment pot. If using SRS, count those investments once and allow for access dates and withdrawal tax.</li><li>Review annually. Match the next spending years with cash and bond maturities as retirement gets closer.</li></ol><p class="result-footnote">An example ${money(e.topup)} eligible top-up now could grow to ${money(e.early)} by 55, versus ${money(e.later)} if delayed ${e.delay} years, at an assumed 4%. Actual eligibility and liquidity come first.</p>${e.housingShortfall?`<p class="result-footnote">Your housing entry exceeds available OA by ${money(e.housingShortfall)} across the projection; that needs another funding source.</p>`:""}<a class="text-link dark-link" href="https://www.cpf.gov.sg/member/tools-and-services/calculators" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Check personalised CPF payouts \u2197</a></details>
